WebCore: no curl alt-svc cache file.

curl writes the alt-svc cache back through a temporary file and a rename when a request's handle is
cleaned up, a rename per request; on LazyOS's ext2 volume a rename flushes every dirty block twice under
the VFS lock. Alt-svc only redirects to protocols this curl does not use (HTTP/3).

--- a/Source/WebCore/platform/network/curl/CurlContext.cpp
+++ b/Source/WebCore/platform/network/curl/CurlContext.cpp
@@ -558,6 +558,14 @@
 
 void CurlHandle::enableAltSvc()
 {
+#if PLATFORM(LAZYOS)
+    // LazyOS: curl keeps the alt-svc cache in a file it reads when a request starts and writes back,
+    // through a temporary file and a rename, when the request's handle is cleaned up: a rename for every
+    // request, and on an ext2 volume without a journal each file rename orders itself with two flushes of
+    // every dirty block of the volume. A page with hundreds of requests held the filesystem for most of a
+    // second at a time. Alt-svc only redirects to other protocols (HTTP/3) this curl does not use.
+    return;
+#endif
     if (!CurlContext::singleton().isAltSvcEnabled())
         return;
 
